---
source: crates/trust-cg-test/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help_of(&[\"ratchet\", \"tests\"])"
---
Monotonic pass-count ratchet for the workspace test matrix.

Compares the newest JSON in `evals/results/tests/` against
the required `--baseline` JSON. Fails if any `(crate, shard)`
pair in the baseline has a lower `passed` count in the
current run, or a higher `failed` count, or has disappeared
entirely. New shards are OK — the baseline only grows.

Exit codes:
  0 — current run is at or above baseline on every pair.
  1 — regression detected.
  2 — tooling error (missing files, parse error, etc.).

# Examples

  trust-cg-test ratchet tests --baseline path/to/tests-baseline.json
  trust-cg-test ratchet tests --current current.json --baseline baseline.json
  trust-cg-test ratchet tests --baseline path/to/tests-baseline.json --format json

Usage: trust-cg-test ratchet tests [OPTIONS] --baseline <PATH>

Options:
      --current <PATH>
          Override the "current" test-matrix JSON. Default: newest `*.json` under
          `evals/results/tests/`

  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (human, json, junit)

          Possible values:
          - human: Pretty table + narrative, targeted at humans
          - json:  Machine-readable JSON
          - junit: JUnit XML for CI consumers

          [default: human]

      --baseline <PATH>
          Baseline JSON to compare against. Required because v0.1.0 ships no universal
          machine-independent pass-count baseline

  -o, --out <PATH>
          Override the command-specific output file or directory.

          See the selected subcommand's help for its output type and default.

      --timeout <SECS>
          Per-unit timeout in seconds. Subcommands may apply per-unit defaults when this is unset

      --parallel <N>
          Worker count (honors cargo-serialization lock). Default: auto

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress progress bars; errors still go to stderr

  -v, --verbose...
          Show debug-level events. Repeat for more: -vv, -vvv

      --no-cache
          Ignore proof / corpus caches

      --dry-run
          Print what would run without executing external tools

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
